    {
      "id": "INVALID-GUEST-OUTPUT",
      "reason": "The real community guests always return well-formed output, so a community Driver's invalid guest output (InvalidGuestOutput) needs a new guest Component, and an ABI- or manifest-invalid release needs a malformed release fixture; this profile proves only the invalid pin, registration and denied-capability release refusals of either isolation class and, through PCF-CPH-003, the first-party invalid-draft refusals",
      "owner": "#637"
    },
    {
      "id": "OTHER-RESOURCE-LIMITS",
      "reason": "PCF-CPH-010 exhausts a community release through its memory budget only; the signed-release test world fixes the fuel, host-call and output budgets of a release, and the real guests make one host call and emit one small Event, so the fuel, host-call and output limits of a community Driver on the real worker need a release shape with those budgets or a new guest Component",
      "owner": "#637"
    }
  ],
